## Part 1 — Facts, Rules, and Recursion (Session 10)
1. When I asked the Oracle whether reachable(Entrance, TreasureRoom), the answer came back TRUE.

2. The line reachable(X, Y) :- tunnel(X, Y). is the base case because it stops immediately when there is a direct tunnel.
  The line reachable(X, Y) :- tunnel(X, Z), reachable(Z, Y). is the recursive case because it calls itself again with a new chamber Z. It is recursive since the rule keeps repeating until it either finds the goal or runs out of tunnels.

