## Part 4 — Synthesis

9. To a 10‑year‑old: Both the recursive rule and the stack search are like two costumes for the same idea. One is written like a recipe (“if there’s a tunnel, go deeper”), and the other is acted out step by step with a backpack stack. Both mean: keep going forward until you can’t, then backtrack.

10. Real-world use: Exploring a computer’s file system. DFS goes into one folder, then into subfolders, as deep as possible. If it reaches a folder with no more files, it backtracks to the previous folder and continues. It’s the same “go deep, then backtrack” principle.
